1
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:13,013
[♪ opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,556
[bird screeching]

3
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:40,666
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

4
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:53,470
[gasps]

5
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:57,015
[♪ tense music playing]

6
00:01:16,118 --> 00:01:18,453
Get your hands off of her!

7
00:01:18,537 --> 00:01:19,913
[gasps]

8
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:21,415
[both grunting]

9
00:01:27,838 --> 00:01:29,756
You bastard!

10
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:35,095
[Navier] Brother!

11
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:39,433
What? "Brother"?

12
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:42,561
Yes, I am her brother, you swine!

13
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:44,896
Ah, Kosair, what on earth are you doing?

14
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:47,024
Who is this punk?

15
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:49,026
He's Prince Heinrey
of the Western Kingdom.

16
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:50,736
How dare he embrace you, huh?

17
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:53,363
He's a friend.

18
00:01:53,447 --> 00:01:55,991
Friend or not, the only ones
who can embrace you

19
00:01:56,074 --> 00:01:58,201
is me and that son of a bitch, Sovieshu.

20
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:00,245
Please leave right now.

21
00:02:00,329 --> 00:02:01,997
[Navier panting]

22
00:02:10,422 --> 00:02:11,673
[door opens]

23
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:13,008
-Ah.
-Ah.

24
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:15,802
[sighs]

25
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:17,596
My sister.

26
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:19,348
[sighs] Brother.

27
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,729
[exclaims]

28
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:27,272
[panting softly]

29
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,403
[whispers] Go on.

30
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:42,621
[straining] Kosair,
I'm really happy to see you too,

31
00:02:43,288 --> 00:02:44,956
but you're squeezing too tight.

32
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,166
Oh, right. Yes.

33
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:48,043
-Ah, sorry.
-[exhales]

34
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:52,881
You've lost weight.

35
00:02:54,216 --> 00:02:55,217
I have not, Kosair.

36
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,510
Oh, no.

37
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:58,929
You're skin and bones.
You just don't see it.

38
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:00,472
No, I am not.

39
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:02,057
You just don't see it.

40
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,354
Anyway, that bastard.

41
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:10,232
How dare he even look at somebody else?

42
00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:13,110
Ah, so…

43
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:15,028
The box here, is it for me?

44
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:16,279
I'll open it.

45
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:20,200
Will you stop scowling?

46
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:24,162
Ah!

47
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:31,169
Uh, so… what do you think?

48
00:03:31,253 --> 00:03:33,130
Uh… Oh, it's…

49
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:37,008
Uh…

50
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:38,844
It's very…

51
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:44,891
It's very pretty.

52
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:48,311
[laughs] Yes! I knew it!

53
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:52,607
[sighs]

54
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:57,863
The Empress must be
in great distress right now.

55
00:03:58,613 --> 00:03:59,948
[Heinrey] Hmm.

56
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,742
Although her brother
did just try to kill me.

57
00:04:02,826 --> 00:04:04,619
Why would… Wait. Hold on a minute.

58
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,205
-Are you saying that her brother is here?
-Hmm.

59
00:04:07,289 --> 00:04:09,916
Her Majesty's brother, General Kosair?
That one?

60
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:13,044
The same general who's undefeated?

61
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,172
He's won every fight, you know.

62
00:04:16,131 --> 00:04:17,924
I just said I was almost killed.

63
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:19,384
You're alive, so it's fine.

64
00:04:19,468 --> 00:04:21,344
So, tell me, when did he get here?
Why did he come here?

65
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:22,429
What is he doing here?

66
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:23,889
Oh, uh, what?

67
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:25,432
When is he leaving? Huh?

68
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,684
I just told you I was nearly skewered!
He was…

69
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:29,352
[imitates sword swishing]
…swinging it like this.

70
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:31,772
If I hadn't dodged it,
the sword would have…

71
00:04:31,855 --> 00:04:33,023
[grunts] I almost died!

72
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:34,399
Yes, I see. Good.

73
00:04:34,483 --> 00:04:36,443
If I go this way,
he's just over there? [squeals]

74
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:37,903
Wait! Are you crazy?

75
00:04:37,986 --> 00:04:39,529
If you go now, he'll kill you.

76
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:41,239
I don't care if I die
if it's him that kills me.

77
00:04:41,323 --> 00:04:42,324
-No.
-I have to see!

78
00:04:43,074 --> 00:04:44,326
What can I do for you?

79
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:46,036
You came here for me.

80
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:47,287
That is all you can do.

81
00:04:48,914 --> 00:04:49,956
So, that girl…

82
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:52,834
She's even expecting his brat?

83
00:04:52,918 --> 00:04:54,377
[sighs] Brother…

84
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:55,545
The walls have ears.

85
00:04:55,629 --> 00:04:56,630
Watch what you say.

86
00:04:57,589 --> 00:04:59,132
That's not how I act.

87
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,009
Well, then…

88
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:03,220
I suppose I should kill
the two of them right now!

89
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:04,346
[sighs] Stop this, please.

90
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:06,723
You'll be sentenced to death.
Don't be a fool.

91
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:08,099
You cannot threaten the Emperor.

92
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,688
I should have come sooner.

93
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:19,820
How lonely it must have been
all by yourself.

94
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,241
I cannot remain Empress…

95
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:26,868
if I cannot endure this.

96
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:28,745
Okay.

97
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:36,044
[♪ majestic music playing]

98
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:38,797
Your Majesty Navier,
Empress of the Eastern Empire,

99
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:42,300
Kosair, Commander of the North,
humbly reports his return.

100
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:48,640
By Your Majesty's command,
I have defeated the Springwater Bandits,

101
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:51,351
established a village
for the enemies who surrendered,

102
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:54,020
and I have done all I could
to guarantee peace.

103
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,815
You have guarded our empire.

104
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:59,568
Your hard work
has helped our citizens thrive.

105
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:03,113
The New Year's Ceremony was a success,
thanks to you.

106
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,162
Your empire is proud.

107
00:06:11,246 --> 00:06:13,290
I know Sovieshu is grateful.

108
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,418
He will award you the highest honor.

109
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:21,715
[door opens]

110
00:06:38,648 --> 00:06:41,234
I, Kosair, Commander of the North,

111
00:06:41,318 --> 00:06:42,903
offer greetings upon my return.

112
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:48,992
So you've returned in good health?

113
00:06:49,868 --> 00:06:51,328
[spits] I'm pleased.

114
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:58,627
I hear that there have been
no further threats.

115
00:06:58,710 --> 00:07:01,713
Your Majesty has no concerns
and is, in fact, flourishing.

116
00:07:02,297 --> 00:07:04,966
I think that perhaps
I secured the borders too well.

117
00:07:07,761 --> 00:07:08,887
[grunts softly]

118
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,397
The look in your eyes, the same as always.

119
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:20,482
Ever insolent…

120
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:21,650
General.

121
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:23,318
[Kosair grunts softly]

122
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:26,613
This look in my eyes

123
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:28,657
is the one that had
the Springwater Bandits

124
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,200
pissing and shitting in fear.

125
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:31,660
[exhales softly]

126
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:33,328
-[clicks]
-[Sovieshu] Do you…

127
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:36,164
dare to glare…

128
00:07:36,915 --> 00:07:37,916
[Kosair grunts]

129
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:40,877
…at your Emperor, with those eyes?

130
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:43,254
[grunts]

131
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:47,258
Why would I do that, Your Majesty?

132
00:07:47,759 --> 00:07:49,177
[grunts]

133
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:52,305
As you know,
I swore an oath to Your Majesty

134
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:54,766
that I'd annihilate
the Springwater Bandits.

135
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:59,813
And yet, you yourself failed to honor
the one oath I asked you to swear.

136
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:00,939
To cherish my sis--

137
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,609
Lante!

138
00:08:04,693 --> 00:08:06,361
This concludes the medal-award ceremony.

139
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:11,324
[exhales deeply]

140
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:16,329
But there is a banquet with His Majesty…

141
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:17,831
[Kosair sighs exasperatedly]

142
00:08:18,957 --> 00:08:20,458
Emperor!

143
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:22,961
May you always succeed.

144
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,295
And stay alive.

145
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,389
[footsteps receding]

146
00:08:35,724 --> 00:08:38,268
That salute is not traditional.

147
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:41,438
-Why, that--
-Ah, no!

148
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:46,109
I think that I may have seen
some people salute like that in the North.

149
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,779
Get out. Go on, quickly.

150
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:51,573
[sighs]

151
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,053
-[door opens]
-[footsteps receding]

152
00:09:13,136 --> 00:09:14,429
[door closes]

153
00:09:22,645 --> 00:09:24,314
[Rashta breathes deeply]

154
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:27,692
[softly] Your Majesty.

155
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:29,903
[breathes deeply]

156
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:31,112
Were you having a nightmare?

157
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:36,576
Lay down, please. Hold Rashta.

158
00:09:38,036 --> 00:09:40,205
[breathes deeply]

159
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:52,133
Have you felt the child?

160
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:53,760
Does it move in your womb?

161
00:09:55,470 --> 00:09:58,389
You know, the imperial physician said
there's a long way before that.

162
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:00,683
When you do eventually feel it move,

163
00:10:01,518 --> 00:10:02,769
you will tell me, won't you?

164
00:10:04,521 --> 00:10:05,563
Yes.

165
00:10:06,106 --> 00:10:08,358
I will tell you straight away,
Your Majesty.

166
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:09,442
[Sovieshu] Hmm.

167
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:14,114
I will instruct Anton right away…

168
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:16,574
to write a lullaby.

169
00:10:18,785 --> 00:10:22,622
[Sovieshu humming]

170
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,916
[both chuckle]

171
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:29,045
This is your first.

172
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:32,715
Your first child. Aren't you afraid?

173
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:40,181
[♪ ominous music playing]

174
00:10:42,559 --> 00:10:44,018
[Lotteshu] <i>Your child is alive.</i>

175
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:47,897
-[whimpering]
-You don't…

176
00:10:47,981 --> 00:10:49,566
believe me, do you?

177
00:10:51,526 --> 00:10:52,902
Shall I show you?

178
00:10:54,362 --> 00:10:56,156
[Lotteshu laughs]

179
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:04,914
There's no reason to be.

180
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:09,586
Why would I be afraid…

181
00:11:10,628 --> 00:11:11,921
with you by my side?

182
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:17,177
[Sovieshu] Rashta.

183
00:11:18,303 --> 00:11:19,304
Yes?

184
00:11:20,013 --> 00:11:21,598
[Sovieshu] I want to thank you.

185
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:25,810
Thank you for having my child.

186
00:11:26,728 --> 00:11:29,147
Anything you desire is yours.

187
00:11:30,273 --> 00:11:32,775
Whether it is something you wish to eat,

188
00:11:32,859 --> 00:11:35,570
something that you wish to have, anything.

189
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:36,738
Just tell me.

190
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:40,825
Honestly?

191
00:11:41,326 --> 00:11:42,535
[Sovieshu] Of course.

192
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:45,413
The mother has to be happy

193
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:48,833
for the child in the womb
to be happy also.

194
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:56,257
What's the matter?

195
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:01,054
I'm so content. [sobs softly]

196
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:05,808
I'm crying from happiness.
[inhales sharply]

197
00:12:06,893 --> 00:12:08,144
[Sovieshu] Hmm.

198
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:25,328
[gasps]

199
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:28,289
Oh, good heavens! [gasps]

200
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:34,087
[gasps] Good heavens!

201
00:12:34,671 --> 00:12:39,175
Even Madam Duchess Joubert sent a gift,
congratulating us on your pregnancy.

202
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:41,386
Oh, how cute! [chuckles]

203
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:46,015
This ironclad stronghold looks like
it is starting to break.

204
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:48,685
[gasps] Good.

205
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:52,146
Hmm. What do you suppose this is?

206
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:53,231
[Albani] What?

207
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:58,194
[Charles] It looks like hair.

208
00:12:58,278 --> 00:12:59,904
[Albani] Hair? Well, who's it from?

209
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:04,158
[Philomena] Hmm. There's no separate mark
to show who sent it.

210
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:05,743
There's something inside.

211
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:08,871
[Albani] Read it.

212
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:11,833
[Philomena] "This is Ian's hair."

213
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,334
[Albani] Ian?

214
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:16,754
"We called your baby 'Ian'…"

215
00:13:16,838 --> 00:13:18,214
[♪ ominous music playing]

216
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:24,679
[clears throat]

217
00:13:26,472 --> 00:13:28,558
[door opens, then closes]

218
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:32,562
"We called your baby 'Ian,' Rashta.

219
00:13:33,688 --> 00:13:35,356
"As you know, he's a boy.

220
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,607
"He looks like you.

221
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:40,820
"His brownish hair is exactly like yours."

222
00:13:43,114 --> 00:13:44,240
[gasps]

223
00:13:45,283 --> 00:13:47,160
[breathing shakily]

224
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:49,996
[box thuds]

225
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:52,081
[♪ music swells]

226
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,589
Is this true, Rashta?

227
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:02,633
[breathing raggedly]

228
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:06,220
I asked you a question.

229
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:07,805
[panting]

230
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,981
[♪ music fades]

231
00:14:24,322 --> 00:14:26,324
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

232
00:14:27,325 --> 00:14:28,910
[Lotteshu] Ah!

233
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:32,121
-There he is! Here you are!
-Ah, look who it is!

234
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:33,289
There we go.

235
00:14:34,499 --> 00:14:36,125
My dear grandson!

236
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:37,752
[grunts]

237
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:41,964
Anyone could tell that it's Rashta's baby.
They look exactly alike! Exactly!

238
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:45,009
I'm telling you, Rashta's looks
were stamped all over that baby's face.

239
00:14:45,093 --> 00:14:46,719
-Goodness.
-[Charles] What are we going to do?

240
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:49,806
If we just sit back and do nothing,
something terrible is bound to happen.

241
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:50,932
Firstly…

242
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:52,683
Rashta can go to the palace

243
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,435
-and offer 500,000 crans.
-Ah.

244
00:14:54,519 --> 00:14:56,187
Take the promissory note!

245
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,647
[groans]

246
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:59,148
Good heavens! Ugh!

247
00:15:00,108 --> 00:15:02,401
Can we be certain
the baby that Rashta carries

248
00:15:02,485 --> 00:15:04,320
is actually the Emperor's child?

249
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:08,825
She played innocent.

250
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:11,994
Never told anyone she had a lover before
and deceived us.

251
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,872
How do we know there are no other lies?

252
00:15:14,956 --> 00:15:17,125
[gasps] Hold your tongue!

253
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,293
Do you even hear yourself, girl?

254
00:15:19,377 --> 00:15:21,337
Oh, it definitely is his!

255
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,048
[sighs deeply] Goodness!

256
00:15:24,132 --> 00:15:25,424
[gasps] You!

257
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:27,176
If I hear those words
from your mouth again,

258
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:28,678
best believe I'll sew it shut!

259
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:29,762
[groans]

260
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:31,389
[sighs frustratedly]

261
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:33,558
[♪ unsettling music playing]

262
00:15:35,852 --> 00:15:37,186
[jewelry clinking]

263
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:39,355
[Lotteshu] Good girl.

264
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,276
Your necklace.

265
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:44,861
[scoffs]

266
00:16:10,678 --> 00:16:13,681
[Sovieshu humming]

267
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:27,945
[pen scratching]

268
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:32,033
Tell me, is it not delightful?

269
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,410
It is a lullaby for my child.

270
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:37,622
[Prime Minister] Most impressive,
Your Majesty. Once again, congratulations.

271
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:41,125
-[Minister of Finance] Congratulations.
-[ministers] Congratulations.

272
00:16:45,213 --> 00:16:46,297
It's lovely.

273
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:50,509
This New Year's Ceremony
is a great success.

274
00:16:51,761 --> 00:16:52,970
It's all thanks to you.

275
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:58,434
As for the New Year's budget,
there are no major changes, but--

276
00:16:58,517 --> 00:17:02,772
Any changes will be
to Rashta's allowance and for the child.

277
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:06,108
I want you to search
for the most skilled midwives

278
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:07,652
in the Eastern Empire.

279
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:09,528
Select about 10.

280
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:23,584
[♪ gentle music playing]

281
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:33,636
[Heinrey] Your Majesty.

282
00:17:42,979 --> 00:17:43,980
[chuckles softly]

283
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:46,315
[chuckles]

284
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:48,526
Your Highness!

285
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:51,112
Your steps seem rather hurried.

286
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:52,989
I've had so much to do…

287
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:54,615
and foolishly forgot to eat.

288
00:17:54,699 --> 00:17:55,783
I'm hurrying to dinner.

289
00:17:56,701 --> 00:17:58,077
What brings you two here?

290
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,704
The party. I was invited.

291
00:18:00,288 --> 00:18:01,539
The party?

292
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:06,460
My brother's welcome party.

293
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:07,795
It was a secret, was it not?

294
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:09,672
You and Sir Kosair think alike.

295
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,674
Although it looks like he got there first.

296
00:18:12,675 --> 00:18:14,010
[both chuckling]

297
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:15,344
[chuckles softly]

298
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:18,598
[Kosair laughs] There!

299
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:19,807
Surprised?

300
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:23,102
Today, your dear brother
is going to treat everyone who loves you,

301
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:24,937
my wonderful sister.

302
00:18:25,021 --> 00:18:26,022
Sit down.

303
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,070
Uh…

304
00:18:36,324 --> 00:18:39,869
The great ruler who crushed
the Springwater Bandits.

305
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:41,954
I truly admire you, sir.

306
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:44,332
This is a gift.

307
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,416
I hope you like wine.

308
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:50,254
And who… might you be?

309
00:18:50,338 --> 00:18:51,422
Ah…

310
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:52,632
I serve…

311
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:54,550
I serve as First Vanguard
and Storm Assault Captain

312
00:18:54,634 --> 00:18:57,178
under the Wolf Knights of the Corps
of Lions Capital First Defense Command.

313
00:18:57,261 --> 00:19:00,306
Also known as the lonely, spotted,
and colorful scarlet leopard cat

314
00:19:00,389 --> 00:19:01,766
of the Himalayan mountains.

315
00:19:02,767 --> 00:19:03,976
I am McKenna.

316
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:05,853
[exclaims excitedly]

317
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:07,938
What Kenna?

318
00:19:08,439 --> 00:19:10,274
Uh… McKenna, sir,
is what you can call me.

319
00:19:10,358 --> 00:19:11,942
Ah, MenKenna.

320
00:19:12,026 --> 00:19:13,152
No, Mc…

321
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:14,236
McKenna.

322
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,613
-[giggles]
-[Kosair] MenKenna.

323
00:19:15,696 --> 00:19:16,864
It's Mc.

324
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:18,491
Mc.

325
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:20,201
-Sit down.
-Yes.

326
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:26,874
This is a valuable beverage
I brought especially for you, my friends.

327
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:30,878
It is a drink designed
to hearten the souls of the battlefield.

328
00:19:31,796 --> 00:19:33,089
I present this bottle to you,

329
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:36,425
and we'll drink to the happiness
of my sister, Empress Navier!

330
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:37,968
-[pops]
-[laughing]

331
00:19:38,052 --> 00:19:40,805
[guests chuckling and clapping]

332
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:44,433
-[liquid trickling]
-I'd wager that this is the first instance

333
00:19:44,517 --> 00:19:46,977
Navier has ever called anyone a friend.

334
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:53,484
-Leopard Cat!
-Ah, yes! Leopard Cat, McKenna.

335
00:19:53,567 --> 00:19:54,610
-Have some.
-Thank you, sir.

336
00:19:54,694 --> 00:19:56,404
[Navier chuckles]

337
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:02,410
I would like to pour you a drink.

338
00:20:02,493 --> 00:20:03,494
[laughs]

339
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:07,289
Now then, to my sister, the Empress.

340
00:20:07,373 --> 00:20:08,416
Cheers!

341
00:20:22,847 --> 00:20:23,889
[exhales]

342
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:26,976
Oh. [laughs]

343
00:20:29,562 --> 00:20:30,563
Oh, oh, oh!

344
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:32,189
Wait a minute. Stop there, wait.

345
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:35,609
This soup is made
with very rare mushrooms.

346
00:20:36,861 --> 00:20:37,862
Try it.

347
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:39,905
Oh, no, no, no.

348
00:20:39,989 --> 00:20:40,990
Ah, eat this too.

349
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:42,658
Eliza, sorry.

350
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:43,951
Oh! Wait, wait, wait.

351
00:20:44,034 --> 00:20:45,661
-This too.
-It's too much, Kosair!

352
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,496
You should know,
these are very rare mushrooms

353
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,290
which only grow at the border
after snowfall.

354
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:53,210
Sir Kosair climbed the cliff himself
to forage a few for Your Majesty to try.

355
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:56,881
[exclaiming]

356
00:20:57,465 --> 00:20:58,591
[Kosair] This too.

357
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:01,093
-[guests laugh]
-You have to eat it all.

358
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:05,681
You…

359
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:08,934
Please forgive me.

360
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:10,853
[chuckling]

361
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:12,646
[Laura] Now, don't push until I tell you.

362
00:21:12,730 --> 00:21:13,898
[McKenna] I won't.

363
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,399
[Laura] Ready, set…

364
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:17,443
go!

365
00:21:19,737 --> 00:21:22,114
What's this? Is this your idea of pushing?

366
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,700
That is disappointing, General.

367
00:21:26,494 --> 00:21:27,995
Now, I'll count one, two, three.

368
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,331
So try pushing. Ready? One, two, three!

369
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,415
-Oh!
-[cackling]

370
00:21:31,499 --> 00:21:33,501
-[all laughing]
-But I…

371
00:21:33,584 --> 00:21:34,585
-Colorful!
-Wait!

372
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,420
Scarlet, mm, leopard cat! [laughs]

373
00:21:36,504 --> 00:21:39,089
Ah, wait a moment.
Just wait one moment. Ah!

374
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:40,549
[groans in pain]

375
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:42,218
-[Kosair] Round two.
-[Laura] Sit down once again.

376
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:44,678
-[McKenna] I'll try from the inside out.
-Shall we get some air?

377
00:21:44,762 --> 00:21:46,722
[Falhan] I'm afraid
Sir Kosair is unbeatable!

378
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:52,269
Heinrey…

379
00:21:53,229 --> 00:21:55,815
I heard you will return
to the Western Kingdom soon.

380
00:21:58,067 --> 00:22:00,319
-[sighs deeply]
-McKenna mentioned it.

381
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:04,865
Is your brother's illness quite serious?

382
00:22:07,034 --> 00:22:09,578
His condition has worsened, I'm afraid.

383
00:22:09,662 --> 00:22:11,664
But there's no reason for concern yet.

384
00:22:13,582 --> 00:22:15,292
I wanted to ask you a question.

385
00:22:16,961 --> 00:22:17,962
Ask away.

386
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:22,925
Your husband…

387
00:22:24,885 --> 00:22:25,886
Do you…

388
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:27,972
Do you love him?

389
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:42,361
[♪ poignant music playing]

390
00:22:52,621 --> 00:22:54,540
If Sovieshu felt joy…

391
00:22:57,251 --> 00:22:59,295
I would also be joyous.

392
00:23:02,339 --> 00:23:03,632
We had a bond.

393
00:23:05,593 --> 00:23:07,761
Our pains and triumphs were shared.

394
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:15,728
I had thought it would last forever.

395
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:17,313
[sighs softly]

396
00:23:20,274 --> 00:23:21,901
That can no longer be.

397
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:52,056
[♪ gentle music playing]

398
00:24:27,383 --> 00:24:28,592
[sighs deeply]

399
00:24:31,053 --> 00:24:32,179
Why don't you take revenge?

400
00:24:35,683 --> 00:24:36,725
Pardon?

401
00:24:37,643 --> 00:24:40,896
You could take a very beautiful,
high-ranking man as your lover.

402
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:41,981
To show him.

403
00:24:44,233 --> 00:24:46,026
I know if you were my lover…

404
00:24:47,194 --> 00:24:48,904
Sovieshu may lose his sanity.

405
00:24:49,655 --> 00:24:50,823
I didn't say me, did I?

406
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:54,326
[chuckles softly]

407
00:24:57,329 --> 00:24:58,539
Your glass is empty.

408
00:25:01,709 --> 00:25:03,335
[both chuckle softly]

409
00:25:03,419 --> 00:25:04,586
[Navier clears throat]

410
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:06,755
Well, then…

411
00:25:08,549 --> 00:25:09,591
Well, what?

412
00:25:10,676 --> 00:25:11,885
One…

413
00:25:11,969 --> 00:25:14,972
very beautiful, high-ranking,
remarkable man.

414
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:17,433
Currently single.

415
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:18,642
[laughs]

416
00:25:18,726 --> 00:25:19,727
[chuckles]

417
00:25:20,853 --> 00:25:22,521
The ceremony this year…

418
00:25:24,857 --> 00:25:26,358
I will never forget it.

419
00:25:26,442 --> 00:25:28,819
[♪ music continues playing]

420
00:25:43,834 --> 00:25:46,754
[Kosair] Some former Springwater Bandits
even sent me a couple of puppies.

421
00:25:46,837 --> 00:25:50,424
They were so tiny, I could hold them both
in one hand! [exclaims]

422
00:25:50,507 --> 00:25:53,260
Navier, I really wish
you could have seen them.

423
00:25:53,343 --> 00:25:55,637
[both laughing]

424
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:57,347
You are such a sweet man.

425
00:25:57,973 --> 00:25:59,683
Why have you found no one yet?

426
00:26:00,851 --> 00:26:03,062
Marquess, do you know the reason?

427
00:26:03,145 --> 00:26:06,065
Well, Your Majesty,
whenever he sees a pretty woman,

428
00:26:06,148 --> 00:26:08,984
he becomes so shy
that he freezes like a wooden doll.

429
00:26:09,610 --> 00:26:10,944
That cannot be true.

430
00:26:11,028 --> 00:26:14,990
He breaks into a cold sweat, cannot speak,
and his expression is…

431
00:26:15,074 --> 00:26:17,367
Hmm. Looks just like that.

432
00:26:19,203 --> 00:26:20,204
[shushes]

433
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:23,040
-Who is it?
-What do you see?

434
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:32,424
[Falhan] That woman, isn't she…

435
00:26:33,926 --> 00:26:35,260
It's Sovieshu's mistress.

436
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:38,472
So, that's her.

437
00:26:47,481 --> 00:26:49,108
I was just out taking a stroll.

438
00:26:49,942 --> 00:26:53,028
I was told to walk often.
The physician recommended it.

439
00:26:53,904 --> 00:26:57,950
Our child is already very fussy
and is a terribly picky eater.

440
00:26:58,659 --> 00:27:01,703
My morning sickness is awful.
There's only one thing I can eat.

441
00:27:01,787 --> 00:27:03,664
Just apple pie, nothing else.

442
00:27:03,747 --> 00:27:06,542
As you know, Your Majesty, apple pie is--

443
00:27:06,625 --> 00:27:08,252
It is His Majesty's favorite food.

444
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:09,545
[giggles]

445
00:27:09,628 --> 00:27:12,714
Exactly. Imagine when he heard that news…

446
00:27:12,798 --> 00:27:13,799
[Navier] All right.

447
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:16,385
Be sure to take care.

448
00:27:19,138 --> 00:27:21,014
Rashta's aware you look down on her.

449
00:27:23,016 --> 00:27:24,268
Rashta understands.

450
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:28,647
The pregnancy celebration invite
was rejected too.

451
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:31,233
Don't be jealous, Your Majesty.

452
00:27:31,942 --> 00:27:33,110
It's unbecoming of you.

453
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:37,322
What?

454
00:27:37,823 --> 00:27:39,783
You think me less than you.

455
00:27:39,867 --> 00:27:42,327
No matter how much
your malice shines through,

456
00:27:42,411 --> 00:27:43,871
Rashta will keep enduring.

457
00:27:45,414 --> 00:27:47,082
I do respect you so.

458
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:48,667
Therefore…

459
00:27:50,127 --> 00:27:52,004
I choose not to fight with you any longer.

460
00:27:52,087 --> 00:27:53,839
It is for the benefit of my child.

461
00:27:55,716 --> 00:27:56,758
Why do you say that?

462
00:27:57,342 --> 00:27:59,720
Lady Albani told me all there is to know.

463
00:27:59,803 --> 00:28:02,598
How you may, in fact, be infertile

464
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:06,602
and will likely be the adoptive mother
of the child that Rashta now carries.

465
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:10,188
What?

466
00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:11,940
Girl…

467
00:28:16,987 --> 00:28:18,864
Say that again.

468
00:28:20,282 --> 00:28:21,867
What are you babbling about?

469
00:28:23,535 --> 00:28:25,913
Well, Her Majesty was the one who first…

470
00:28:28,332 --> 00:28:29,333
"Adoptive…

471
00:28:32,085 --> 00:28:33,545
"mother"?

472
00:28:35,130 --> 00:28:36,340
Stop it, brother.

473
00:28:36,423 --> 00:28:37,883
[gasps softly]

474
00:28:37,966 --> 00:28:39,927
That is my sister.

475
00:28:40,010 --> 00:28:41,470
[gasps] I didn't, I…

476
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:43,430
-[Kisia] Oh no, Ms. Rashta!
-[Cherini] Are you all right?

477
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:45,098
Why, you little…

478
00:28:45,182 --> 00:28:46,683
-Oh no!
-Oh no.

479
00:28:46,767 --> 00:28:48,101
Sir Kosair, leave her.

480
00:28:48,185 --> 00:28:50,187
-You must not get provoked.
-[Rashta] The baby!

481
00:28:50,270 --> 00:28:51,730
-You…
-Ah, my stomach hurts.

482
00:28:51,813 --> 00:28:54,775
Say one more word about my Navier
being an adoptive mother,

483
00:28:54,858 --> 00:28:56,109
or raising your little brat,

484
00:28:56,193 --> 00:28:59,321
by my honor, I shall rip the tongue
from your lying mouth!

485
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:00,656
[Falhan] Let's go, Kosair!

486
00:29:01,990 --> 00:29:03,158
[Cherini] Are you all right?

487
00:29:03,241 --> 00:29:06,495
-Your Majesty, please, you must go.
-[Kisia] It's going to be all right.

488
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:08,330
[breathing raggedly]

489
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:09,790
-[Kisia] Hurry, hurry.
-What happened here?

490
00:29:09,873 --> 00:29:11,458
-Over here. The baby!
-Are you all right?

491
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:13,168
-What do we do?
-You have to help the baby now.

492
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:15,379
[♪ dramatic music playing]

493
00:29:15,462 --> 00:29:17,547
-Can you stand?
-Oh dear.

494
00:29:18,131 --> 00:29:19,800
[moaning]

495
00:29:40,028 --> 00:29:41,029
[weakly] Your Majesty.

496
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:44,700
Do not fear, my Rashta.

497
00:29:45,409 --> 00:29:46,576
I am here by your side.

498
00:29:47,369 --> 00:29:48,745
How is the child doing?

499
00:29:49,454 --> 00:29:50,872
Does that matter

500
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:52,666
at a time like this?

501
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:56,628
Rashta cares a lot for the baby.

502
00:29:58,338 --> 00:30:01,216
I think that you are far more important.

503
00:30:02,592 --> 00:30:03,802
Oh.

504
00:30:06,346 --> 00:30:07,347
A damp cloth.

505
00:30:18,025 --> 00:30:19,860
I'd like to talk with you outside.

506
00:30:26,283 --> 00:30:27,284
How is she?

507
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:29,953
She needs rest until she has recovered.

508
00:30:30,579 --> 00:30:31,913
Is it anything serious?

509
00:30:31,997 --> 00:30:34,499
[physician] In the early stages
of pregnancy, one must be careful.

510
00:30:34,583 --> 00:30:36,793
Ms. Rashta was never strong to begin with.

511
00:30:37,335 --> 00:30:40,047
If she is not careful,
then she could suffer a miscarriage.

512
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:41,715
So this cannot happen again.

513
00:30:43,341 --> 00:30:45,302
[exhales heavily]

514
00:30:47,387 --> 00:30:49,014
[sighs furiously]

515
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:52,225
[grunts]

516
00:30:54,102 --> 00:30:55,729
[vase clanking]

517
00:30:57,898 --> 00:30:59,524
[breathing shakily]

518
00:30:59,608 --> 00:31:00,609
[exhales]

519
00:31:12,579 --> 00:31:14,498
The physician said
not to worry about anything.

520
00:31:18,335 --> 00:31:20,253
Would you hold my hand?

521
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:30,013
I heard you went to the garden…

522
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:33,141
and saw the Empress and General Kosair.

523
00:31:36,269 --> 00:31:37,354
[exhales shakily]

524
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:39,606
He screamed as if he wanted to kill me.

525
00:31:40,357 --> 00:31:42,984
I fell after he pushed me.

526
00:31:43,068 --> 00:31:44,653
He was intimidating and threatening.

527
00:31:44,736 --> 00:31:45,862
It was scary.

528
00:31:47,823 --> 00:31:48,824
Pushed you?

529
00:31:54,162 --> 00:31:55,163
Is that true?

530
00:31:57,165 --> 00:31:59,000
-It is, yes.
-[gasps] Hmm?

531
00:32:00,043 --> 00:32:01,294
[whispers] What…

532
00:32:02,087 --> 00:32:04,589
-What…
-You must tell His Majesty the truth.

533
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:16,101
Yes, it's true, Your Majesty.

534
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:17,644
[sighs]

535
00:32:23,316 --> 00:32:25,068
The child is what angered him.

536
00:32:26,069 --> 00:32:28,947
He does not want Rashta
to have Your Majesty's baby.

537
00:32:29,030 --> 00:32:30,031
[breathes shakily]

538
00:32:31,158 --> 00:32:33,118
The Empress looked at me with such…

539
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:34,661
cold eyes.

540
00:32:34,744 --> 00:32:36,079
It was frightening.

541
00:32:36,163 --> 00:32:37,914
She felt the same as her brother.

542
00:32:40,375 --> 00:32:41,918
And that is the truth.

543
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:48,550
[♪ foreboding music playing]

544
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,370
Kosair is banished from the palace?

545
00:33:17,454 --> 00:33:19,414
They say it is His Majesty's order.

546
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:23,710
"As an investigation has begun
into the assault against Ms. Rashta,

547
00:33:23,793 --> 00:33:25,921
"Sir Kosair is to leave the palace."

548
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:27,005
[gasps]

549
00:33:27,088 --> 00:33:28,965
"He is to wait outside the palace walls

550
00:33:29,716 --> 00:33:31,968
"until his punishment is decided."

551
00:33:32,052 --> 00:33:34,888
[groans] Sovieshu, that son of a bitch.

552
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:36,223
The order makes no sense.

553
00:33:36,932 --> 00:33:40,018
I'll march out there
and butcher every soldier in my way

554
00:33:40,101 --> 00:33:42,145
just to explain it to that bastard.

555
00:33:42,229 --> 00:33:44,439
-[Eliza] Please restrain yourself, sir.
-General!

556
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:47,067
-Step aside.
-Should you choose to fight…

557
00:33:47,734 --> 00:33:49,277
I will stand beside you as always.

558
00:33:49,361 --> 00:33:52,072
But it puts Her Majesty
into a complicated situation.

559
00:33:56,451 --> 00:33:57,452
[Kosair groans angrily]

560
00:34:02,374 --> 00:34:04,042
Arrest him.

561
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:05,627
Just try.

562
00:34:18,223 --> 00:34:19,641
[groans angrily]

563
00:34:20,684 --> 00:34:22,227
They claimed it was assault?

564
00:34:22,811 --> 00:34:25,730
They say that the general
pushed Rashta, Your Majesty.

565
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:28,066
[sighs in disbelief]

566
00:34:41,788 --> 00:34:42,789
[door closes]

567
00:34:43,748 --> 00:34:44,749
[exhales]

568
00:34:45,625 --> 00:34:46,668
It is Rashta.

569
00:34:47,502 --> 00:34:48,837
She claims she was pushed.

570
00:34:49,379 --> 00:34:51,172
My brother did not touch her.

571
00:34:51,256 --> 00:34:52,424
[exhales]

572
00:34:52,507 --> 00:34:53,842
She is mistaken.

573
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:55,927
I witnessed it all.

574
00:34:56,845 --> 00:34:58,388
Her report is not true.

575
00:34:58,471 --> 00:34:59,848
And my brother is innocent.

576
00:35:00,432 --> 00:35:01,891
[sighs]

577
00:35:01,975 --> 00:35:03,435
You expect me to believe that?

578
00:35:03,518 --> 00:35:07,063
I have always been honest with you.
Do you believe I would lie, Your Majesty?

579
00:35:07,147 --> 00:35:09,232
It is already decided.

580
00:35:09,316 --> 00:35:12,110
Kosair was seen pushing her by witnesses.

581
00:35:13,903 --> 00:35:15,780
Your Majesty has lost his eyes and ears.

582
00:35:15,864 --> 00:35:18,116
I nearly lost my child!

583
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:21,077
It is not important if Rashta lied or not.

584
00:35:21,161 --> 00:35:22,746
The problem is you.

585
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:26,499
You refuse to accept and acknowledge
that I am having a baby.

586
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:28,918
Your cold animosity…

587
00:35:29,628 --> 00:35:32,756
it reveals a blatant truth
within your being.

588
00:35:32,839 --> 00:35:35,508
Kosair was moved to act this way
because of you.

589
00:35:38,178 --> 00:35:39,679
And you should know that…

590
00:35:40,263 --> 00:35:43,558
this decision is my consideration for you.

591
00:35:47,771 --> 00:35:49,397
How very charitable of you.

592
00:35:52,025 --> 00:35:53,485
This is a warning.

593
00:35:54,194 --> 00:35:56,279
You will cease your hostility at once.

594
00:35:57,197 --> 00:35:59,908
If anything like this happens
to my child again, then I will not…

595
00:36:01,493 --> 00:36:02,869
forgive Kosair.

596
00:36:05,538 --> 00:36:07,123
And I will not forgive you.

597
00:36:08,708 --> 00:36:10,710
[♪ tense music playing]

598
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:42,701
[Rashta] You clearly saw the Empress'
older brother push me, didn't you?

599
00:36:42,784 --> 00:36:44,536
Listen, you must tell the truth!

600
00:36:44,619 --> 00:36:46,121
[hesitatingly] I don't know.

601
00:36:46,204 --> 00:36:47,497
I don't think I saw anything.

602
00:36:47,580 --> 00:36:48,623
He pushed Rashta!

603
00:36:48,707 --> 00:36:49,708
He absolutely did.

604
00:36:49,791 --> 00:36:51,751
He pushed Rashta.
He pushed me, and you saw.

605
00:36:51,835 --> 00:36:54,713
-And that is the truth. Do you understand?
-Yes, I understand, Ms. Rashta.

606
00:36:54,796 --> 00:36:56,548
-[door opens]
-[Kisia] Ms. Rashta!

607
00:36:57,173 --> 00:37:00,343
Her Majesty's older brother
has been ordered out the palace.

608
00:37:00,427 --> 00:37:02,178
The knights seized him
and dragged him away.

609
00:37:02,262 --> 00:37:04,931
And they say
that His Majesty scolded the Empress,

610
00:37:05,014 --> 00:37:07,308
and she was driven out in tears.

611
00:37:07,392 --> 00:37:08,476
Really?

612
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:11,020
[exhales]

613
00:37:12,147 --> 00:37:13,148
[sighs in relief]

614
00:37:14,107 --> 00:37:15,275
[door closes]

615
00:37:15,942 --> 00:37:16,943
Your Highness,

616
00:37:17,485 --> 00:37:18,737
where are you going?

617
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:20,905
Sir Kosair was chased out of the palace.

618
00:37:20,989 --> 00:37:22,073
Your Highness…

619
00:37:27,746 --> 00:37:29,581
A letter has arrived from our homeland.

620
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:34,961
[♪ somber music playing]

621
00:37:39,549 --> 00:37:42,218
HIS MAJESTY KING WALTON III
IS IN CRITICAL CONDITION

622
00:37:44,471 --> 00:37:45,472
I should…

623
00:37:46,931 --> 00:37:47,974
return now.

624
00:37:49,309 --> 00:37:50,727
That decision is wise.

625
00:37:51,311 --> 00:37:52,937
Your ascension is guaranteed.

626
00:37:53,021 --> 00:37:56,441
And the next successor after you
is far removed.

627
00:37:56,524 --> 00:37:59,736
But it would still be best
for you to return quickly.

628
00:38:01,571 --> 00:38:02,697
To hear the final words.

629
00:38:10,455 --> 00:38:12,123
-[door opens]
-[sighs heavily]

630
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:13,625
[door closes]

631
00:38:20,507 --> 00:38:22,509
[♪ wistful music playing]

632
00:38:52,789 --> 00:38:53,832
Here you are.

633
00:38:53,915 --> 00:38:55,250
I've been looking for you.

634
00:38:56,209 --> 00:38:57,377
What do you need?

635
00:38:57,460 --> 00:39:00,713
Marquess Lante has news
from the Western Kingdom, Your Majesty.

636
00:39:01,297 --> 00:39:03,633
Their king is said to be critically ill.

637
00:39:06,761 --> 00:39:08,137
His kingdom needs him.

638
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:10,431
Prince Heinrey must return.

639
00:39:10,515 --> 00:39:11,933
I'm afraid he must.

640
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:14,978
His delegation will leave tonight,
Your Majesty.

641
00:39:15,645 --> 00:39:17,313
Since invitees
fall under your jurisdiction--

642
00:39:17,397 --> 00:39:18,773
As soon as possible?

643
00:39:20,441 --> 00:39:21,568
Yes.

644
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,948
Will you bid him farewell?

645
00:39:36,291 --> 00:39:37,333
I think not.

646
00:39:39,878 --> 00:39:41,629
It is not wise to do so.

647
00:39:44,424 --> 00:39:47,385
Lady Eliza, do everything in your power

648
00:39:47,468 --> 00:39:49,095
to ensure his safe return.

649
00:39:49,178 --> 00:39:52,140
Yes. I will, Your Majesty.

650
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:05,069
[sighs]

651
00:40:12,243 --> 00:40:13,244
[chirps softly]

652
00:40:15,496 --> 00:40:17,498
[♪ gentle music playing]

653
00:40:34,891 --> 00:40:39,020
It is my honor to meet you, my queen.

654
00:40:40,021 --> 00:40:42,774
Are you a good dancer, Your Majesty?

655
00:40:47,195 --> 00:40:49,739
[Navier] <i>If you are sharing your thoughts</i>
<i>through these letters,</i>

656
00:40:49,822 --> 00:40:51,157
<i>why meet at all?</i>

657
00:40:51,240 --> 00:40:54,911
They are too special.
I must meet that person.

658
00:40:55,745 --> 00:40:57,914
<i>Your Majesty, I'm so glad it was you.</i>

659
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:00,500
<i>I really mean it.</i>

660
00:41:02,251 --> 00:41:04,545
[Navier] <i>I was so thrilled</i>
<i>that it was you.</i>

661
00:41:07,674 --> 00:41:09,342
<i>I'm so grateful.</i>

662
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:30,113
<i>Prince Heinrey, your friendship</i>
<i>has healed many wounds</i>

663
00:41:30,196 --> 00:41:32,365
<i>I would not have been able to treat alone.</i>

664
00:41:35,535 --> 00:41:37,537
<i>You are a truly good person.</i>

665
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,165
[♪ music continues playing]

666
00:41:41,249 --> 00:41:42,625
[sighs heavily]

667
00:41:44,836 --> 00:41:47,714
[Heinrey] <i>I did not know</i>
<i>our parting would come so soon.</i>

668
00:41:53,970 --> 00:41:56,973
[Navier] <i>I wonder</i>
<i>how many more opportunities there will be</i>

669
00:41:57,056 --> 00:41:59,517
<i>for us to meet in this lifetime.</i>

670
00:42:07,567 --> 00:42:10,153
<i>Goodbye, Heinrey.</i>

671
00:42:21,748 --> 00:42:22,749
[♪ music fades]

672
00:42:30,298 --> 00:42:31,966
[Albani] They say that if a man eats this,

673
00:42:33,301 --> 00:42:34,927
his seed will dry up.

674
00:42:35,428 --> 00:42:38,139
For a woman, her field will be unfruitful.

675
00:42:38,723 --> 00:42:41,601
She'd be infertile
for the rest of her life.

676
00:42:41,684 --> 00:42:43,686
[♪ ominous music playing]

677
00:42:52,028 --> 00:42:53,279
Keep this secret…

678
00:42:54,113 --> 00:42:55,990
until it is all over.

679
00:42:57,158 --> 00:42:58,576
With the stars as our witness,

680
00:42:59,494 --> 00:43:01,913
your secret will be safe here.

681
00:43:01,996 --> 00:43:04,165
Only the two of us will know,
Your Majesty.

682
00:43:04,248 --> 00:43:05,374
[door opens]

683
00:43:05,458 --> 00:43:09,045
Your Highness, Lady Navier,
please don't run.

684
00:43:10,004 --> 00:43:11,506
[chuckling]

685
00:43:12,673 --> 00:43:14,217
That dear child…

686
00:43:17,095 --> 00:43:18,679
is destined to lead us.

687
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:21,724
Soon, all the Mistresses will arrive.

688
00:43:21,808 --> 00:43:24,352
[Albani] I will have them
prepared with tea.

689
00:43:25,686 --> 00:43:28,064
I have faith
those wenches will enjoy them.

690
00:43:28,147 --> 00:43:30,191
[Albani] Do not worry, Your Majesty.

691
00:43:47,792 --> 00:43:49,794
[♪ music continues playing]

692
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:27,415
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

693
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:29,500
[♪ closing theme music playing]
